# Ownership boundaries for review routing.
#
# The split: application code (site/) is open to any contributor — CI is the
# gate there. Infrastructure and the deploy pipeline are owned, because a
# mistake in them doesn't fail a test, it changes DNS or ships to production.
# PRs touching owned paths auto-request review from the owner; with branch
# protection's "require review from Code Owners" enabled, that review blocks
# the merge for those paths only.
#
# Note the deeper guardrail behind this file: contributors have no Cloudflare
# tokens and no Pulumi stack access. Even a merged change to infra/ does
# nothing until an infra owner runs `pulumi up` locally.

/infra/            @ramanshrivastava
/.github/          @ramanshrivastava
/site/wrangler.jsonc  @ramanshrivastava
